            "id": "4a1669d8-5076-36dc-ba62-53cd2e63043d",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "PepsiCo revamp: What to expect from the activist investor deal",
            "description": "<p>PepsiCo (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/PEP\">PEP</a>) agreed to lower prices and cut costs in a deal with activist investor Elliott Management.</p>\n<p>Yahoo Finance Senior Reporter <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/ines-ferre/\">Ines Ferr\u00e9</a>, Siebert Financial chief investment officer Mark Malek, and Principal Asset Management chief global strategist Seema Shah join Opening Bid host <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/brian-sozzi/\">Brian Sozzi</a> to discuss the deal and what it signals about the broader consumer staples sector (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/XLP\">XLP</a>).</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/opening-bid/\">Opening Bid</a>.</p>",
            "summary": "PepsiCo (PEP) agreed to lower prices and cut costs in a deal with activist investor Elliott Management. Yahoo Finance Senior Reporter Ines Ferr\u00e9, Siebert Financial chief investment officer Mark Malek, and Principal Asset Management chief global strategist Seema Shah join Opening Bid host Brian Sozzi to discuss the deal and what it signals about the broader consumer staples sector (XLP). To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more Opening Bid.",
