            "id": "6bda32c5-81a5-35d2-9e9d-c7854e4f17a1",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "How Nvidia selling in China helps 'propel the market forward'",
            "description": "<p>President Trump <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/trump-approves-nvidia-h200-chips-for-sale-to-china-203937120.html\">announced on Monday</a> that he has approved Nvidia (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/NVDA\">NVDA</a>) selling H200 chips in China.</p>\n<p>Siebert Financial chief investment officer Mark Malek sits down with Morning Brief host <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/julie-hyman/\">Julie Hyman</a> to discuss what the easing export controls mean for Nvidia and the broader artificial intelligence (AI) industry.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/morning-brief/\">Morning Brief</a>.</p>",
            "summary": "President Trump announced on Monday that he has approved Nvidia (NVDA) selling H200 chips in China. Siebert Financial chief investment officer Mark Malek sits down with Morning Brief host Julie Hyman to discuss what the easing export controls mean for Nvidia and the broader artificial intelligence (AI) industry. To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more Morning Brief.",
